In article <n9142247.744458262@honeydew> n9142247@honeydew.cc.wwu.edu (Gus Iverson) writes:
>Ok the first one did not work so I will try again.
>  I am running 3.1.3 on my 486 running DOS 6. My problem is that the
>opening screen where it tells you the story of the game is garbage. It
>seems to be full of color codes or some such. Any suggestions? Thanks in
>advance.

try adding

DEVICE=C:\DOS\ANSI.SYS
(or some better ansi driver)
to your config.sys file.  NetHack needs ansi

Also try (if you're not already) installing ChrHack to get a better
looking NetHack.  (Still need Ansi.sys though)

>  One more question, Anyone out there compiled their own version on a PC?
>Which compilor did you use? Has anyone had any success with the djpp
>adaptation of the GNU C compilor? (I would like to know before I try it
>myself)
>
Yep, I compiled NH with djgpp.  Worked first time.  Make sure that your
files are in the MSdos format (not the unix format), that you edit the
makefile to use the right directories, and you set the environment
variables for the gnu libraries.
(The docs for installing Nethack and installing Gcc are very helpful)

Takes about an hour on a 486/50dx (not dx2).

